course: dictionary
lesson: 937
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so context decides which one you need. «In the Blitz German planes bombed British cities, and many children were evacuated to the countryside.» Bombing and evacuation tell you that the Blitz is a time in history.
explain: «We had a blitz on the bedroom before Gran came round.» There are no planes here. The clue is the quick tidying, so a blitz means a big, fast effort to get something done.
explain: Blitz can also be a verb, an action word. «Blitz the strawberries in the blender» means whizz them up very quickly. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: The Blitz means the heavy German bombing of British cities, especially London, in 1940–1941 during the Second World War.
fact: A blitz can also mean a sudden, strong attack, such as a fast rush attack in sport.
fact: «A cleaning blitz» is an informal phrase for a big, fast effort to tidy or clean.
fact: «Blitz it» means to whizz food quickly in a blender.
fact: Blitz is short for Blitzkrieg, a German word meaning lightning war.
exercise: «In the Blitz German planes bombed British cities.» What is the Blitz? | A type of blender | *A time of heavy German bombing of British cities in 1940–1941 | A quick way to clean the kitchen | A famous spelling test
exercise: Mum says, «Let's have a cleaning blitz before Gran arrives.» What does blitz mean here? | A bomb falling on the house | *A big, fast effort to get the house tidy | A long, lazy nap | A slow walk round the garden
exercise: Ella reads, «Blitz the carrots in the blender.» What does blitz mean? | *Whizz them up quickly | Peel them slowly | Wrap them in paper | Freeze them for a month
test: «The team made a blitz down the wing, and the other side could not stop them.» What does blitz suggest? | *A sudden, strong attack | A slow, gentle walk | A long rest at half time | A quiet, sleepy game
test: «They blitzed the room in ten minutes.» What does blitzed mean? | Left it untouched | Lost it under the bed | *Cleaned or tidied very quickly | Painted very slowly
exam: «Sirens wailed through the night during the Blitz, so families hid in air-raid shelters.» Using the clues, what does the Blitz mean? | A quick cleaning job at home | A setting on a blender | A slow walk in the countryside | *The heavy German bombing of British cities in the Second World War
